## Architecture & Theory

### Appium Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Test Client                              │
│  (Java, Python, JavaScript, Ruby, etc.)                    │
└────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                     │
        ┌────────────▼────────────────┐
        │   HTTP/JSON Wire Protocol   │
        └────────────┬────────────────┘
                     │
┌────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Appium Server                                  │
│  - Routes commands to drivers                              │
│  - Manages sessions                                        │
│  - Handles logging                                         │
└────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                     │
        ┌────────────┴─────────────┐
        │                          │
    ┌───▼────┐              ┌─────▼────┐
    │ Android│              │   iOS    │
    │ Driver │              │  Driver  │
    └───┬────┘              └──┬──────┘
        │                      │
    ┌───▼────────────┐     ┌───▼─────────┐
    │ ADB (Android)  │     │ XCUITest    │
    │ UIAutomator    │     │ (iOS)       │
    └─────────────────┘     └─────────────┘
        │                      │
    ┌───▼────────────┐     ┌───▼─────────┐
    │ Android Device │     │ iOS Device  │
    │ or Emulator    │     │ or Simulator│
    └─────────────────┘     └─────────────┘
```

### How Appium Works

**Step-by-Step Process:**

```
1. Test Client sends command via HTTP
   ↓
2. Appium Server receives request
   ↓
3. Server routes to appropriate driver (Android/iOS)
   ↓
4. Driver translates to platform-specific commands
   ↓
5. Commands sent to device/emulator via ADB (Android) or XCUITest (iOS)
   ↓
6. Device executes command
   ↓
7. Response sent back through same chain
   ↓
8. Test client receives result
```

### Appium Server Endpoints

**Main REST API Endpoints:**

```
POST /wd/hub/session              → Create new session
GET /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}   → Get session details
DELETE /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}→ Delete session (quit)

POST /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}/element    → Find element
POST /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}/elements   → Find elements

POST /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}/element/{elementId}/click
POST /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}/element/{elementId}/clear
POST /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}/element/{elementId}/value
POST /wd/hub/session/{sessionId}/element/{elementId}/text
```

