## Desired Capabilities

### Theory

Desired Capabilities are a set of key-value pairs that describe the requirements for a test session. They tell the Appium server what kind of session you want to start.

### Common Capabilities

**Android Capabilities:**
```java
UiAutomator2Options options = new UiAutomator2Options();

// Required capabilities
options.setDeviceName("Android Device");           // Device name
options.setPlatformName("Android");               // Platform
options.setPlatformVersion("11");                 // OS version

// App information
options.setApp("/path/to/app.apk");               // App path
options.setAppPackage("com.example.app");         // Package name
options.setAppActivity(".MainActivity");          // Main activity

// Optional capabilities
options.setAutoGrantPermissions(true);            // Auto grant permissions
options.setNewCommandTimeout(300);                // Command timeout (seconds)
options.setNoReset(true);                         // Don't reset app state
options.setFullReset(false);                      // Don't uninstall app
options.setChromedriverExecutable("/path/to/chromedriver"); // For Chrome/WebView
options.setMaxSessions(1);                        // Max parallel sessions
```

**iOS Capabilities:**
```java
XCUITestOptions options = new XCUITestOptions();

// Required capabilities
options.setDeviceName("iPhone 13");               // Device name
options.setPlatformName("iOS");                   // Platform
