## Locator Strategies

### Theory

Locator strategies are methods to find elements in an app. Different strategies work better in different scenarios.

### Locator Types

**1. ID (Resource ID - Android)**
```java
// Android - Resource ID
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("com.example:id/button_login"));

// Best for: Android apps with unique IDs
// Pros: Fast, reliable, unique
// Cons: Not available on iOS
```

**2. AccessibilityID**
```java
// Both Android and iOS
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.accessibilityId("Logout Button"));

// Best for: Both platforms, accessibility testing
// Pros: Works on both, semantically meaningful
// Cons: May not always be unique
```

**3. ClassName**
```java
// Find element by class name
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.className("android.widget.Button"));

// Best for: Android native elements
// Pros: Available for all native elements
// Cons: Often not unique, multiple same types
```

**4. XPath**
```java
// Absolute XPath
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.xpath(
    "//android.widget.Button[@text='Login']"
));

// Relative XPath
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.xpath(
    "//XCUIElementTypeButton[@name='Login']"
));

// XPath with predicates
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.xpath(
    "//android.widget.LinearLayout[@resource-id='com.example:id/container']/android.widget.Button[1]"
));

// Best for: Complex selections, cross-platform
// Pros: Powerful, flexible
// Cons: Fragile to UI changes, slower
```

**5. Predicate String (iOS)**
```java
// iOS predicate string
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.iOSNsPredicateString(
    "type == 'XCUIElementTypeButton' AND name == 'Login'"
));

// Complex predicate
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.iOSNsPredicateString(
    "type == 'XCUIElementTypeTextField' AND value BEGINSWITH 'Enter'"
));

// Best for: iOS-specific testing
// Pros: Native iOS approach, powerful
// Cons: iOS only
```

**6. Class Chain (iOS)**
```java
// Class chain locator
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.iOSClassChain(
    "**/XCUIElementTypeButton[`name == 'Login'`]"
));

// Complex class chain
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.iOSClassChain(
    "**/XCUIElementTypeWindow[1]/XCUIElementTypeButton"
));

// Best for: iOS element hierarchy navigation
// Pros: Efficient, hierarchical
// Cons: iOS only
```

**7. Android DataMatcher**
```java
// Android data matcher for list items
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.androidDataMatcher(
    "hasEntry(name, \"John\")"
));

// Best for: Android DataMatcher-enabled apps
// Pros: Access to adapter data
// Cons: Limited to specific apps
```

### Locator Strategy Comparison

| Strategy | Android | iOS | Speed | Reliability | Notes |
|----------|---------|-----|-------|-------------|-------|
| ID | ✅ | ❌ | ⚡⚡ | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Fastest for Android |
| AccessibilityID | ✅ | ✅ | ⚡⚡ | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Best cross-platform |
| ClassName | ✅ | ✅ | ⚡⚡ | ⭐⭐⭐ | Often not unique |
| XPath | ✅ | ✅ | ⚡ | ⭐⭐⭐ | Flexible but fragile |
| Predicate | ❌ | ✅ | ⚡⚡ | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | iOS native approach |
| Class Chain | ❌ | ✅ | ⚡⚡⚡ | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Fastest for iOS |

### Locator Best Practices

**Good Locator:**
```java
// ✅ Good - Specific, stable, accessible
WebElement loginButton = driver.findElement(
    AppiumBy.accessibilityId("login_button")
);

WebElement emailField = driver.findElement(
    AppiumBy.id("com.example:id/email_input")
);
```

**Bad Locator:**
```java
// ❌ Bad - Generic, fragile, slow
WebElement element = driver.findElement(
    AppiumBy.xpath("//android.widget.LinearLayout[3]/android.widget.Button[2]")
);

// ❌ Bad - Hardcoded coordinates
WebElement element = driver.findElement(
    AppiumBy.xpath("//XCUIElementTypeButton[@x='100' and @y='200']")
);
```

