## Element Interactions

### Common Element Operations

**Finding Elements:**
```java
// Find single element
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("element_id"));

// Find multiple elements
List<WebElement> elements = driver.findElements(AppiumBy.className("android.widget.Button"));

// Wait for element (will cover in Wait Strategies section)
WebElement element = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.presenceOfElementLocated(AppiumBy.id("element_id"))
);
```

**Click Operations:**
```java
// Simple click
WebElement button = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("button_id"));
button.click();

// Multiple clicks
button.click();
button.click();

// Double click using W3C Actions
Actions actions = new Actions(driver);
actions.doubleClick(button).perform();

// Long press
actions.clickAndHold(button)
    .pause(Duration.ofSeconds(2))
    .release()
    .perform();
```

**Text Input:**
```java
// Clear and type
WebElement emailField = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("email_input"));
emailField.clear();
emailField.sendKeys("user@example.com");

// Type without clearing
emailField.sendKeys(" - additional text");

// Get current text
String currentText = emailField.getText();
System.out.println("Email: " + currentText);
```

**Attribute Access:**
```java
// Get element attributes
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("element_id"));

String id = element.getAttribute("resource-id");
String text = element.getAttribute("text");
String contentDesc = element.getAttribute("content-desc");

// Check if element is displayed
boolean isDisplayed = element.isDisplayed();

// Check if element is enabled
boolean isEnabled = element.isEnabled();

// Get tag name
String tagName = element.getTagName();

// Get element location
Point location = element.getLocation();
System.out.println("X: " + location.x + ", Y: " + location.y);

// Get element size
Dimension size = element.getSize();
System.out.println("Width: " + size.width + ", Height: " + size.height);
```

**Element Scrolling:**
```java
// Scroll to element (Android)
((AppiumDriver) driver).executeScript(
    "mobile: scrollGesture",
    ImmutableMap.of(
        "left", 100,
        "top", 100,
        "width", 200,
        "height", 200,
        "direction", "down",
        "percent", 3.0
    )
);

// Scroll in a specific view
scrollInView("android.widget.ListView", "down", 5);

// iOS scroll
((AppiumDriver) driver).executeScript(
    "mobile: scroll",
    ImmutableMap.of("direction", "down")
);
```

