## Wait Strategies

### Theory

Waits are crucial in mobile testing because:
- Network latency
- App loading time
- Animation delays
- Asynchronous operations

Three types of waits:
1. **Implicit Wait** - Default wait for all operations
2. **Explicit Wait** - Wait for specific conditions
3. **Fluent Wait** - Custom polling interval and timeout

### Implicit Wait

```java
@Before
public void setUp() {
    // Apply implicit wait to all operations
    driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(10));
}

// Now every findElement will wait up to 10 seconds
WebElement element = driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("element_id"));
```

**Pros:**
- Simple to implement
- Applies globally

**Cons:**
- Fixed timeout
- Can mask timing issues
- Waits for all operations

### Explicit Wait

```java
// Standard Explicit Wait
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));

// Wait for element presence
WebElement element = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.presenceOfElementLocated(AppiumBy.id("element_id"))
);

// Wait for element visibility
WebElement element = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(AppiumBy.id("element_id"))
);

// Wait for element clickability
WebElement button = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(AppiumBy.id("button_id"))
);
button.click();

// Wait for element invisibility
boolean invisibile = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.invisibilityOfElementLocated(AppiumBy.id("loading_spinner"))
);

// Wait for specific text in element
WebElement element = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.textToBePresentInElementLocated(
        AppiumBy.id("message_label"),
        "Success"
    )
);
```

**Pros:**
- Flexible conditions
- Specific to operation
- Better error messages

**Cons:**
- More verbose
- Need to write custom conditions

### Fluent Wait

```java
// Custom polling with fluent wait
FluentWait<WebDriver> fluentWait = new FluentWait<>(driver)
    .withTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(10))        // Max wait time
    .pollingEvery(Duration.ofMillis(500))       // Check every 500ms
    .ignoring(NoSuchElementException.class)     // Ignore these exceptions
    .ignoring(StaleElementReferenceException.class);

WebElement element = fluentWait.until(
    driver -> driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("element_id"))
);
```

### Custom Wait Conditions

```java
// Custom wait condition class
public class CustomWaitConditions {
    public static ExpectedCondition<WebElement> elementToHaveText(
            By locator, String text) {
        return driver -> {
            WebElement element = driver.findElement(locator);
            if (element.getText().contains(text)) {
                return element;
            }
            return null;
        };
    }

    public static ExpectedCondition<Boolean> elementToBeStable(
            WebElement element) {
        return driver -> {
            Point location1 = element.getLocation();
            try {
                Thread.sleep(100);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }
            Point location2 = element.getLocation();
            return location1.equals(location2);
        };
    }
}

// Usage
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebElement element = wait.until(
    CustomWaitConditions.elementToHaveText(
        AppiumBy.id("status_label"),
        "Loading"
    )
);
```

### Wait Best Practices

```java
// ✅ Good - Explicit wait for specific condition
WebElement loginButton = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(AppiumBy.id("login_button"))
);
loginButton.click();

// ❌ Bad - Hardcoded sleep
Thread.sleep(5000);
driver.findElement(AppiumBy.id("login_button")).click();

// ✅ Good - Wait for element with specific text
WebElement message = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.textToBePresentInElementLocated(
        AppiumBy.id("message_label"),
        "Success"
    )
);

// ✅ Good - Wait for element to disappear
wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.invisibilityOfElementLocated(AppiumBy.id("loading"))
);
```

